  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.6776. The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder, multiprofile over singleprofile, avgpool over transformer (0.5907 vs 0.5191 for PCA), and weighted over concat fusion (0.6776 vs 0.6315). The one untested dimension that could plausibly push beyond 0.6776 is the image encoder: ResNet50 alone scored very poorly (0.2079), suggesting it may be a weak contributor even in fusion. config_037 swaps only the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings identical to config_031 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted). This isolates the effect of image representation quality. If ViT-L provides a stronger visual signal, the weighted fusion should benefit more, potentially exceeding the current best. With only 1 experiment remaining after this, this single-variable exploitation of the most promising untested axis is the highest-expected-value choice."
}

